    <string name="lh_about_steps">Steps are counted by your watch throughout the day. Any movement counts, from a walk to the shops to a run.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_calories">Calories burned through activity, on top of what your body uses at rest.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_cardio">Moderate activity counts once and vigorous activity counts double toward your weekly goal. Health organisations recommend at least 150 minutes a week.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_resting_hr">Your heart rate while you are still and relaxed. A lower resting heart rate usually means better cardiovascular fitness.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_hrv">The variation in time between heartbeats, measured during sleep. Compare it with your own baseline rather than with others.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_readiness">How ready your body is for a hard effort, based on sleep, recovery and recent training.</string>
    <string name="lh_about_weight">It\'s normal for your weight to go up and down during the day, depending on what you eat and drink.</string>
